{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>איתי</b> — there is." "<b>די מנית יתהון</b> — like: whom the chief of the eunuchs appointed. Now there is a question: there is no doubt that Daniel was the most distinguished, and we know that he did not bow to the idol. Why did the Chaldeans not mention him to the king? In my opinion: because they feared to mention him, since they knew that the king offered incense before him as is done for his gods. Yefet ben Eli said: they were his friends, therefore they did not mention him. And this is unnecessary."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:35.981169303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}